---
title: Message markup
sidebar:
  order: 4
---

Tag names and their arguments aren't case sensitive. Numbers can be decimal or hexadecimal, such as `10` or `0x0A`. A tag that isn't on this page is an error.

## Printing

| Tag | What it does |
| --- | --- |
| `[BR]` | Ends the line. |
| `[Wait]` | Waits for the player to press A. |
| `[Next]` | Moves on to a new page of the box. |
| `[Scroll 2]` | Scrolls the text up by 2 lines. |
| `[Pause 10]` | Pauses for 10 frames. |
| `[End]` | Ends the message, and closes the box. |
| `[Yield]` | Hands control back to the EVT script that showed the message, and keeps the box open. Comes before `[End]`. |
| `[Speed delay=2 chars=1]` | Prints 1 character every 2 frames. |
| `[DelayOff]`, `[DelayOn]` | Prints the text after `[DelayOff]` all at once, until `[DelayOn]`. |
| `[InputOff]`, `[InputOn]` | Ignores the player's buttons, until `[InputOn]`. |
| `[EnableCDownNext]` | Lets the player press C-Down to move on to the next page. |
| `[RewindOn]`, `[RewindOff]` | No known use. |

## Box styles

`[Style ...]` sets how the box looks, and usually comes first.

| Tag | Box |
| --- | --- |
| `[Style right]` | A speech bubble, with its tail on the right |
| `[Style left]` | A speech bubble, with its tail on the left |
| `[Style center]` | A speech bubble, with its tail in the middle |
| `[Style tattle]` | A tattle |
| `[Style choice pos=120,90 size=75,46]` | A list of options, at a position on the screen, at a size. See [Choices](/papermario-dx/messages/choices). |
| `[Style inspect]` | A gray box, used when the player inspects something |
| `[Style sign]` | A sign |
| `[Style lamppost height=72]` | A lamppost sign, with the given height |
| `[Style postcard index=0]` | A postcard, showing the given image |
| `[Style popup]` | A small box, such as for getting a partner's shell |
| `[Style popup2]` | Another small box, with no known use |
| `[Style upgrade pos=40,35 size=240,42]` | A box for an upgrade block, at a position on the screen, at a size |
| `[Style narrate]` | Narration, such as "You got a Mushroom!" |
| `[Style epilogue]` | The text at the end of a chapter, with no box |

## Choices

| Tag | What it does |
| --- | --- |
| `[Cursor 0]` | Puts the cursor for option `0` here. |
| `[Option 0]` | Starts the text of option `0`. `[Option 255]` comes after the last option. |
| `[SetCancel 1]` | Picks option `1` when the player presses B. |
| `[EndChoice 2]` | Ends a list of 2 options. |

`[BeginChoice]` numbers the options for you. After it, each `[Option]` with no number puts the cursor and starts the next option, and `[EndChoice cancel=1]` ends the list and picks option `1` when the player presses B:

```
[Style choice pos=120,90 size=75,46]
[BeginChoice]
[Option]Yes[BR]
[Option]No[BR]
[EndChoice cancel=1][End]
```

## Text

| Tag | What it does |
| --- | --- |
| `[Font standard]` | Sets the font: `standard`, `menu`, `menu2`, `title`, or `subtitle`. |
| `[Color red]` | Sets the color of the text, by name or by number, such as `[Color 0x0A]`. |
| `[SaveColor]`, `[RestoreColor]` | Saves the color, and goes back to the saved one. |
| `[Size 32,32]` | Sets the width and height of the characters. |
| `[SizeReset]` | Sets the size of the characters back to normal. |
| `[CharWidth 8]` | Gives every character the same width. `[CharWidth 0]` turns it off. |
| `[FullSpace]`, `[HalfSpace]` | Prints a wide or a narrow space. |

The color names depend on the box's `[Style]`:

| Style | Colors |
| --- | --- |
| `inspect` | `dark` |
| `sign` | `normal`, `red`, `blue`, and `green` |
| `popup` | `normal`, `red`, `pink`, `purple`, `blue`, `teal`, `green`, and `yellow` |
| Any other | `normal`, `red`, `pink`, `purple`, `blue`, `cyan`, `green`, and `yellow` |

## Position

| Tag | What it does |
| --- | --- |
| `[SetPosX 40]`, `[SetPosY 15]` | Moves where the text prints to. |
| `[Right 8]`, `[Down 6]`, `[Up 6]` | Moves where the text prints by a number of pixels. |
| `[CenterX 159]` | Centers the text around a position. `[CenterX 0]` turns it off. |
| `[SavePos]`, `[RestorePos]` | Saves where the text prints, and goes back to the saved place. |

## Effects

An effect applies to the text after it, until its closing tag, such as `[Wave]Hello![/Wave]`. `[/FX]` closes the most recent effect.

| Tag | What it does |
| --- | --- |
| `[Shake]` | Shakes each character. |
| `[Wave]` | Moves each character in a wave. |
| `[Rainbow]` | Colors each character in turn. |
| `[PrintRising]` | Prints each character rising into place. |
| `[PrintGrowing]` | Prints each character growing into place. |
| `[SizeJitter]` | Changes the size of each character at random. |
| `[SizeWave]` | Changes the size of each character in a wave. |
| `[DropShadow]` | Draws a shadow under the text. |
| `[NoiseOutline]` | Draws the text with a noisy outline. |
| `[Static 50]` | Draws static over the text, by an amount. |
| `[Blur dir=xy]` | Blurs the text, in `x`, `y`, or `xy`. |
| `[DitherFade 217]` | Fades the text, by an amount. |

## Images

The image tags show images that an EVT script sets with `SetMessageImages`, by their index in its list.

| Tag | What it does |
| --- | --- |
| `[InlineImage index=0]` | Shows a small image where the text prints. |
| `[Image index=0 pos=85,97 hasBorder=1 alpha=255 fadeAmount=15]` | Shows an image at a position, fading it in. |
| `[HideImage fadeAmount=15]` | Fades the image out by an amount each frame. `[HideImage]` hides it at once. |
| `[ItemIcon itemID=0x0057]` | Shows an item's icon. |
| `[AnimSprite spriteID=0x0039 raster=30]` | Shows a sprite's raster, as a frame of an animation. |
| `[AnimDelay index=0 delay=14]` | Sets how many frames frame `0` of the animation lasts. |
| `[AnimLoop 0 0]` | Repeats the animation. |
| `[AnimDone 0]` | Ends the animation. |

## Inserted text

| Tag | What it does |
| --- | --- |
| `[Var 0]` | Inserts text or a number that an EVT script sets with `SetMessageText` or `SetMessageValue`, from `0` to `2`. |

## Sound

| Tag | What it does |
| --- | --- |
| `[Voice normal]` | Sets the sound the text makes as it prints: `normal`, `bowser`, or `star` (also written `spirit`). |
| `[Volume 50]` | Sets the volume of the text's sound. |

## Special characters

These print a symbol: `[NOTE]`, `[HEART]`, `[STAR]`, `[UP]`, `[DOWN]`, `[LEFT]`, `[RIGHT]`, `[CIRCLE]`, `[CROSS]`, and the button symbols `[A]`, `[B]`, `[L]`, `[R]`, `[Z]`, `[C-UP]`, `[C-DOWN]`, `[C-LEFT]`, `[C-RIGHT]`, and `[START]`.

Each button symbol prints in its button's color. To pick another color, add `color=` to any of them except `[A]` and `[Z]`: `blue`, `green`, `red`, `yellow`, or `gray`, such as `[START color=blue]`. To print a button symbol in the text's color, put `~` before its name, such as `[~A]`.

## Raw bytes

`[Raw 0xFF 0x06]` puts bytes into the message as they are. Use it for message codes that have no tag, such as `0xFF 0x06`, which ignores the player's buttons for the rest of the message.

Don't use `[SetCursorPos]` or `[CustomVoice]`. They have bugs that cause errors.
